    // OoO evidence is a real single-cycle event aligned with the cycle in
    // which the younger instruction is accepted by the functional unit.
    // Loads never enter the issue queue, so the "older load outstanding"
    // condition has to come from the LSU (request presented, response
    // outstanding, or response being consumed).  A registered copy would be
    // one cycle late and can miss the load-wait window entirely.
